# Build context exclusions for api/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile copies go.mod, go.sum, *.go and config.yaml explicitly, so
# nothing listed here is needed by any stage. The compiled binary is the entry
# that matters: `make -C api build` writes it to the context root, where it would
# otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every build.

# Compiled binary produced by `make -C api build` / `go build ./...`. Named `api`
# because the module path ends in `/api`; it sits at the context root and is
# ~34MB. Also ignored by the repository .gitignore as /api/api.
/api

# Component tooling and documentation. None of it is copied into any stage.
/Makefile
/README.md
/.golangci.yaml
/.dockerignore
/Dockerfile

# Go build and coverage artefacts.
*.out
*.test
